% -- konec titulní strany --

\nadpissptakemL{What is {\FYKOS}?}{logo1.eps}{-1mm}{0mm}{2.5cm}

{\FYKOS} is a correspondence-based competition allowing high school
students to broaden their knowledge of physics by solving creative problem sets.
The competition is organized by the Faculty of Mathematics and Physics,
Charles University. The organizing team consists of students as well as
teachers and employees of the faculty. 
Its aim is to strenghten the problem-solving 
skills of high school students and eventually prepare for competitions like IPhO.

{\FYKOS} targets students interested in physics of all types of secondary
(grade~9 to~12 in K-12~system or ISCED 3) education establishments. The participants
should be able to comunicate either in~Czech, Slovak, or English. Every year,
the~organizing team creates and publishes \textbf{six~eight-task problem sets}.
Those intending to participate send their solutions using the {\FYKOS} web
page. Once the organizing team corrects the solutions, they are sent back to
the participants with commentaries on corrections.

\nadpissptakemL{Why participate in {\FYKOS}?}{logo1.eps}{0mm}{0mm}{2.5cm}

Tackling {\FYKOS} problem sets helps participants enlarge their physics 
problem-solving toolkit and get to understand the different concepts in more depth. 
{\FYKOS} can also serve as preparation for other physics-related competitions.

The participants with sufficient point scores are invited to {\FYKOS} camps 
(organised twice a year), where they meet many like-minded peers. Friendships 
created during the camps last through university and even longer. And of course, 
exciting and rewarding prizes await the most successful problem-solvers.

\nadpissptakemL{How to participate in {\FYKOS}?}{logo1.eps}{0mm}{0mm}{2.5cm}

You can find \textbf{the registration form} on our website \url{fykos.org}
along with the information regarding writing and submiting the solution, 
and the evaluation criteria. The websites contain among others the information 
on \textbf{other events} organised by {\FYKOS} or \textbf{the prizes} available. 
Follow us on our \textbf{Facebook} official page \url{http://www.facebook.com/FYKOS}.

